[{"doc_id":3,"user_id":1,"doc_type":"other","text":"other | Resume of Ramesh Das, Senior Full Stack Engineer (SDE III) | RAMESH DAS\nSenior Full Stack Engineer (SDE III) — Node.js | React.js | Go | AWS | GenAI & Agentic AI | Microservices | System Design\nDelhi, India | +91 7059476213 | rameshdas028@gmail.com | LinkedIn\n\nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY\nFull Stack Engineer with 7+ years building high-availability distributed systems on Node.js, React.js, and AWS, with hands-on experience shipping production GenAI/Agentic AI solutions (RAG pipelines, MCP servers, LLM-based automation). Track record of cutting infrastructure cost (~50%) and P99 latency (~60%) while scaling systems to 100K+ RPS and multi-million-record data pipelines. Comfortable owning a system end-to-end — architecture, cloud infra, delivery, and post-launch optimization.\n\nCORE SKILLS\nLanguages: JavaScript (ES6+), TypeScript, Go\nFrontend: React.js, Vue.js, Redux Toolkit, Microfrontends\nBackend: Node.js, Express.js, REST & GraphQL API Design, gRPC\nAI / GenAI: LLMs, AI Agents, Agentic AI, RAG, Prompt Engineering, MCP\nArchitecture: Microservices, Event-Driven, Distributed Systems, System Design\nDatabases: MySQL, MongoDB, DynamoDB, Redis, Elasticsearch\nCloud & DevOps: AWS (Solutions Architect), Terraform, Docker, Kubernetes, GitHub Actions, Jenkins, Serverless\nMonitoring: CloudWatch, Prometheus, Grafana, Loki\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\nFull Stack Developer | SUTRA AI Private Limited (parent of String Ventures) — Noida, India | Nov 2022 – Present\n• Built production GenAI/Agentic AI systems — RAG pipelines, MCP servers, and LLM-based agent workflows — that automate product queries, order tracking, and delivery support for 24/7 customer service.\n• Built an AI-powered document extraction pipeline (LLMs + OCR) converting unstructured documents into structured JSON, cutting manual processing effort by 90%.\n• Designed high-throughput data ingestion pipelines processing 80K–1M records, reducing processing time from ~1 hour to under 5 minutes.\n• Optimized backend APIs, queries, and caching, cutting P90 latency from ~800ms to ~300ms and P99 latency from ~1.5s to ~600ms under high traffic.\n• Designed and implemented a distributed Redis + Lua rate limiter (atomic counters, TTL expiration) enforcing per-client throttling and eliminating API overload and Redis memory growth.\n• Architected and provisioned cloud infrastructure end-to-end (Terraform, Kubernetes, Docker, CI/CD) spanning networking, compute, IAM, load balancing, autoscaling, and monitoring; reduced AWS cost by ~50% with no performance trade-off.\n• Cut Docker build times by 60–90% and manual deployment effort by 70%, enabling zero-downtime production releases.\n• Migrated Redux to Redux Toolkit, cutting boilerplate and lifting frontend state-management performance by ~30%.\n\nSoftware Developer | Volumtree Technology Solutions Pvt. Ltd — Chandigarh, India | May 2022 – Oct 2022\n• Re-architected a Salesforce data pipeline processing ~1.5M records, cutting execution time from days to under 5 minutes.\n• Optimized a React application (memoization, debouncing/throttling, lazy loading, code splitting, tree shaking, virtualization), cutting page load time by 30% and lifting UI responsiveness by 50%.\n• Architected a hybrid SQL + NoSQL data layer for real-time chat, boosting throughput while keeping latency low under high concurrency.\n• Migrated a monolithic application to microservices, improving scalability and fault isolation.\n• Re-engineered product rating aggregation to prevent server overload, cutting server load by 70% and improving customer-facing latency.\n\nSoftware Engineer | RedoQ Ltd (India Office) — Kolkata, India | Oct 2020 – Apr 2022\n• Built scalable restaurant management systems adopted by 5,000+ businesses, cutting customer queue times by 50%.\n• Designed systems handling 100K+ RPS through caching strategies and optimized database access patterns.\n• Migrated legacy Laravel services to Node.js, improving backend performance and long-term maintainability.\n• Implemented gRPC-based inter-service communication for internal microservices, improving service-to-service call performance over REST.\n• Re-architected a monolith from vertical to horizontal scaling using AWS EC2 Auto Scaling and stateless Node.js services, increasing scalability and reducing downtime.\n• Designed a pre-aggregation pipeline for daily/monthly/yearly analytics, eliminating heavy runtime queries and cutting database load.\n• Refactored the rating/review system from bulk updates to single-write patterns, significantly reducing database load.\n\nSoftware Engineer | II Intlum Technology — Kolkata, India | Oct 2019 – Sep 2020\n• Designed and built RESTful and GraphQL APIs supporting core product operations, with Swagger documentation for front-end teams.\n• Built reusable React components (buttons, modals, forms), reducing development time on new features.\n• Replaced offset-based pagination with cursor-based pagination, improving query performance at scale.\n\nEDUCATION\nBachelor of Technology — Electronics and Communication Engineering\nMAKAUT University, West Bengal, India | Jun 2014 – Jul 2018","embedding":[0.009421609,0.03356362,-0.0017161574,0.0035032793,0.002255296,-0.0091503095,-0.028872287,0.0028255752,0.016920196,-0.05793996,-0.039162926,0.013137821,0.04242446,-0.01781602,-0.008127255,-0.020534728,0.024590563,-0.019100403,-0.014766958,0.0061728,0.0051013944,-0.025300477,-0.01734991,0.010679027,-0.0012541892,0.04014954,-0.00881212,-0.021737836,-0.041579627,0.113940336,-0.017097745,-0.0017123863,-0.017749142,-0.0009530565,0.005739905,-0.004867787,-0.020384278,0.013408483,-0.02703275,0.011855073,0.008082883,0.0072636786,-0.0004397827,0.0051203202,0.013488534,0.002668428,-0.010863775,-0.0013120924,0.012611676,-0.020167615,0.0065045995,-0.016214443,0.040445924,0.010814131,-0.011985917,0.016892629,0.0011136294,-0.016741838,0.026535071,-0.003547141,0.008713838,0.0028079348,0.037227426,-0.